### META
directory_path: install/_setup.sh/cli/commands
description: Modular command handlers for dinser CLI per PART 6.5
created: 2025-01-28
modified: 2025-11-29
status: active

### FILES
check.sh | Diagnostic/troubleshooting command per PART 6.3
test.sh | Test suite runner integration per PART 6.5.4
service.sh | Swarm service management per PART 9

### COMMAND_STRUCTURE
Each command file must:
- Define a cmd_<n>() function as entry point
- Include a # description: comment for help text
- Handle --help/-h flags
- Return proper exit codes (0=success, 1=failure)

### ADDING_COMMANDS
To add a new command:
1. Create <command_name>.sh in this directory
2. Define cmd_<command_name>() function
3. Add # description: comment at top
4. dinser will auto-discover the command

### SUBCOMMANDS
For commands with subcommands:
1. Create directory: commands/<command_name>/
2. Add <subcommand>.sh files inside
3. Each defines cmd_<command>_<subcommand>()

### SERVICE_COMMAND_SUBCOMMANDS (per PART 9.7)
list | List all defined services
info | Show service details
build | Build service image
deploy | Deploy to swarm
remove | Remove from swarm
logs | View service logs
status | Check deployment status
check | Run service diagnostics

### DEPENDENCIES
dinser | Parent CLI that sources these modules
